WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.460 --> 00:00:03.220
An order starts as an instruction.

2
00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:08.880
Submission is not proof of acceptance, and acceptance is not proof of a full fill.

3
00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:14.380
A partial fill creates smaller exposure while the remaining order may still be open.

4
00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:21.380
Track the order identifier, fill quantity and current position rather than relying on one status badge.

5
00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:30.180
For an open position, inspect its size and the associated protective orders.

6
00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:35.420
Confirm the intended side, quantity, stop and target on the venue.

7
00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:39.780
Protection can fail or become stale after a size change.

8
00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:47.100
If the dashboard and venue disagree, avoid adding exposure and investigate before modifying the order again.

9
00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:55.320
After an exit, compare the fills and remaining position with the venue.

10
00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:59.180
The journal should explain entry, changes and exit.

11
00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:07.300
Separate realized profit and loss from unrealized estimates, and include fees and funding when reviewing results.

12
00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:11.380
Sample demo performance is not a customer trading record.

13
00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:20.200
A timeout or lost response can occur after the venue accepted an order.

14
00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:24.200
Do not submit a duplicate simply because the page displayed an error.

15
00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:28.440
Check open orders, fills and the known order identifier.

16
00:01:29.180 --> 00:01:34.060
Record the time and error, then follow the recovery procedure or contact support.

17
00:01:38.140 --> 00:01:42.940
Review drawdown, realized results, trade count and costs together.

18
00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:47.700
One winning trade or an attractive chart does not establish performance.

19
00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:51.780
Compare only the same account, network and time range.

20
00:01:52.540 --> 00:01:57.900
Use the review to understand behavior and configuration, not to claim guaranteed future returns.

21
00:02:01.900 --> 00:02:10.480
For an incident, record the workspace, network, timestamp, agent, market and order or transaction identifier.

22
00:02:11.320 --> 00:02:14.220
Include the expected result and what actually happened.

23
00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:17.940
Redact secrets and unnecessary account information.

24
00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:23.780
Confirm current venue exposure and avoid repeated actions until the state is understood.
